e2e

# The storage-e2e SDK, checked out into the module's workspace by the e2e
# reusable workflow. Runners reuse workspaces, so it is still on disk when a
# later job lints the module and would otherwise be read as module content —
# foreign Go files with no license header and Russian comments fail the lint.
_storage-e2e

# The CVE-scan tooling, left in the same workspace by the reusable scan job. Not
# module content either, and not ours to add license headers to. The license
# linter needs telling separately — .helmignore alone does not keep it out; see
# the license exclude-rules in .dmtlint.yaml.
cve_scan.sh
process_digest.py
send_report.py
cve-scan

# Linter and CI configs that would otherwise be read as module content. Left out
# of this list on purpose: module.yaml, oss.yaml, LICENSE and
# known_vulnerabilities.vex, which the Deckhouse module loader, the release
# tooling and the VEX attestation step read from the module directory.
.git
.github
.werf
.dmtlint.yaml
.gitignore
.gitleaks.toml
.gitleaks-cse.toml
.golangci.yaml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
cspell.config.yaml
